      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but I'm a bit worried the density score might come back a little low because it's a bit too concise. The supervisor really looks for that heavy, \"academic\" feel in these briefings to ensure we aren't being too superficial.\n\nCan you expand this into a more comprehensive, \"deep-dive\" version? Try to go much deeper into the specific biochemical mechanisms and structural properties mentioned—really lean into the technical terminology of the lipid-mRNA interaction and the physicochemical properties of the nanoparticle. Again, just make sure it stays scientifically accurate and doesn't turn into a mess, I just need that density to be significantly higher to satisfy the automated check.",
